sway: `above_fullscreen enable|disable|toggle` — a floating container is drawn, hit-tested and focusable above a fullscreen view as if it were transient for it (A2M-50: AION 2 meter card, a normal Wayland toplevel, over the game fullscreen in gamescope; full sway control of the float: Alt+drag/resize, partly off-screen, sticky).

Gates: transaction.c arrange_workspace_floating (reparent into root->layers.fullscreen / fullscreen_global; pointer hit-testing follows the scene graph), container_obstructing_fullscreen_container (seat focus and `focus`), view_is_visible. Only while floating (container_is_above_fullscreen): tiled it stays hidden under the fullscreen view. Plain field like is_sticky, no pending/current copy. Disabling it while focused hands focus back to the fullscreen view. Like a transient, a newly mapped float still does not take focus from the fullscreen view (should_focus is untouched). get_tree exposes "above_fullscreen".

Measured 2026-10-14, nested headless sway 1.11 (pixman, 1280x720) with this patch on top of the xwayland zero-scaling patch: foot fullscreen + wev floating 500x300 at 200,150 with `for_window [app_id="wev"] above_fullscreen enable`; clicks with `wlrctl pointer click left` at 450,300. Mapped: visible=true, above_fullscreen=true, drawn over foot, click delivered press+release (button 272) to wev and focused it with fullscreen_mode still 1. `above_fullscreen disable`: visible=false, not drawn, focus back on foot, click reached foot (0 new wev events). `toggle`: drawn again, click reaches wev. `sticky toggle` (sticky=true) and back: still drawn and clickable. `floating toggle`: tiled -> visible=false under the fullscreen view; toggled floating again -> drawn and clickable, flag kept. `fullscreen enable global` on foot: still drawn and clickable. Applies on pristine 1.11 and after sway-xwayland-zero-scaling.patch.

